（你輕輕碰觸了另一塊石板。你厭惡你自己，你厭惡埃亞爾，你厭惡夏·圖爾人，你厭惡自己身邊的一切事物。你想要摧毀一切，讓億萬死於非命的靈魂的正義得到伸張。你想要滅絕夏·圖爾人——不，不僅如此，你還要滅絕那些一切在他們身邊的東西。精靈、半身人、獸人、人類……一切帶着他們的邪惡印記的人。他們揹負罪惡卻苟活下來，而其他使用傳送門的無辜者卻被烈火灼燒瞬間死於非命。如果埃亞爾上還存在哪怕一個夏·圖爾人，這顆星球都應該被枯萎之火焚燒殆盡。埃亞爾上的一切都應該接受正義的復仇。在你把手從石板上離開了許久之後，你的腦海裏仍然殘存着不明原因的怒火。）

在#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [父親] #{normal}##LAST#的幫助下，我們的#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [匠人] #{normal}##LAST#製造了#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [強力的工具] #{normal}##LAST#，這些被他祝福的#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [修理扳手] #{normal}##LAST#能讓我們#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [搖動地更加劇烈] #{normal}##LAST#。#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [豆子] #{normal}##LAST#們被酸液覆蓋，#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [甜菜] #{normal}##LAST#獲得了超人的速度，#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [胡椒] #{normal}##LAST#用#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [嘈雜的土地] #{normal}##LAST#和他們的雙手融合，射向那些#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [製造噪音] #{normal}##LAST#者。這些#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [花] #{normal}##LAST#有些#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [嘈雜] #{normal}##LAST#，但完全不能和#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [雞蛋怪的尖銳刺耳聲] #{normal}##LAST#相比。如果我們不能#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [成爲能工巧匠] #{normal}##LAST#，我們就會在#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [陽光下凋零] #{normal}##LAST#。按下這塊石板，#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [獲得你的工具箱] #{normal}##LAST#。你將成爲#{italic}##FIREBRICK# [能工巧匠] #{normal}##LAST#。

（一瞬間，你的腦海中回閃出一個酸液樹魔把你的腦袋按在這塊石板上的記憶，你非常瞭解這塊石板是用來幹什麼的。你絕不想要再次碰到這塊石板。）
]], "_t")
t("history of Mal'Rok (1)", "瑪·洛克的歷史（1）", "_t")
t([[First, we were created by our Father, Urh'Rok. Then, many years later, we were in the desert, struggling and fighting each other for the few meager scraps of usable farmland. We do not know anything between these times; our cities, our culture, everything was wiped out by the dust storms. The storms hated us, toyed with us, subsided just long enough for us to raise armies and fight, then raged again the moment peace came. They wanted us to fight. They wanted us to struggle, suffer, die, leaving a few survivors to repopulate, and repeat the process. Green, onyx, red, all brothers who should have been allies, we fought at first because we had to, then because we could, then because we knew it was the only thing that kept the storms entertained.

Eventually, Urh'Rok appeared and told us he had been sealed away, prevented from helping us by people who had been creating the dust storms. Their cities lay hidden among us, shrouded in powerful magic to remain invisible. With a touch, he wiped the storms clean and turned the desert into lush jungle, filled with food. The storms appeared again, weaker this time; Urh'Rok grew furious and shattered the glass cities, reaching into one and pulling out a fistful of sadistic mages. He fed them to us - it was the best, largest feast any of us had eaten in millennia, and it was truly delicious. He did this to all the dust-mages' cities, then declared that we would never have to fear the storms again. We celebrated and worshiped our returned god - thanks to him, we knew where our next meal was coming from, and we had no reason to fight. All of us brethren dropped our weapons and hugged, forgiving each other for the assaults we knew we'd only done from fear. We loved each other, and we loved our god.

Our father began to fret, however. We were supposed to have grown more as species; our squabbling in the desert had stunted our growth, left us behind the curve. He set up a series of competitions and tournaments in all fields of life - magic, combat, negotiation - on a planetary scale. We were used to fighting by now, and now that we knew it was actually accomplishing something, now that we were pleasing an altruistic god, we did not mind it one bit. Those who died did so with smiles on their faces, knowing they'd contributed another data-point to our Father's plan. The weaker members of our many species willingly died off, and we all grew stronger, smarter, and happier as a result. Soon, we were grown enough to organize our own tournaments, and apply the findings to our societies and species; Father said he was pleased with us, and wanted us to determine our own destiny while he slept, recovering from all the work he'd just done. We continued our process of self-improvement - we wanted Father to be proud of us when he woke up.

Then, the Sher'Tul came.
]], [[起初，我們由我們的父親烏魯洛克所創造。在之後的許多年裏，我們都長期居住在無盡的荒漠之中，爲少數幾片可憐的能用於耕作的土地而爭鬥不休。我們不知道任何有關那個時代的事情：我們的城市、我們的文化，所有的這些都被咆哮的塵土風暴捲走了。那些風暴厭惡我們，乃至戲弄我們，它們只有在我們組織軍隊戰鬥的時候纔有短暫的停歇，一旦和平降臨，咆哮而至的風暴瞬間就捲走了一切。他們想要我們不停爭鬥，他們想要我們掙扎，受苦，死亡，只留下少數的倖存者來保存種羣。等到我們從廢墟中重新發展起來，一切依舊。綠翡翠、縞瑪瑙、紅寶石，我們所有的兄弟起初都是盟友，然而我們一開始爲了生存被迫各自爲戰，後來我們只能戰鬥，再到後來，我們的神經已經麻木，戰爭成了連續不斷的風暴間唯一的娛樂活動。

最終，烏魯洛克在我們的面前重現了，他告訴我們，因爲他被長期封印，他不能幫助我們對抗那些製造塵土風暴的罪魁禍首。那些人使用強力的魔法隱藏他們的城市，陰毒地對我們偷偷發動襲擊。烏魯洛克只輕輕一觸，風暴立刻被消散殆盡，荒蕪的沙漠瞬間變成了充滿富足食物的茂密森林。風暴再一次伺機對我們發動偷襲，然而這一次要弱得許多。烏魯洛克異常憤怒，擊碎了那些玻璃城市，將手伸入，抓起一把那些惡毒的法師。他把這些法師當作給我們的食物——啊，那真是千年以來我們所享用過的最大、最豐盛的盛筵。他這樣清除了所有塵埃法師的據點，並向我們宣告——我們再也不用畏懼那些塵土分飽了。我們慶祝着我們偉大的神的歸來——多虧了他，我們再也不會過那些居無定所，食不果腹的生活，也再也不需要互相爭鬥了。我們的同袍紛紛扔下武器互相擁抱，互相原諒了我們過去因爲恐懼而產生的敵對之情。我們互相友愛，而我們更愛我們偉大的神。

然而，我們的父親有些擔心。我們本應該更加茁壯地成長，然而長期在荒漠中的互相爭鬥阻礙了我們的發展，讓我們落後了。他設置了一系列有關生活各個方面的錦標賽——魔法、戰鬥、辯論——在全球範圍內舉行。我們曾經習慣於戰鬥，然而我們現在終於有了戰鬥的目標。爲了讓我們無私的神感到高興，我們什麼都願意做。即使是在比賽中陣亡的人臨死前也懷着滿意的笑容，因爲他的犧牲爲父親和整個種族的發展做出了貢獻。我們的種族中那些弱小的個體們慢慢逝去，而我們變得更加強壯、更加聰明、也更加快樂。最終，我們成長到足夠舉辦我們自己的錦標賽，並把比賽中得出的研究成果應用到我們生活中的方方面面：父親爲我們的行爲感到高興，想要讓我們在他睡着時自己決定自己的命運，通過他給我們的禮物慢慢使我們的種羣從長期的災難中恢復起來。我們繼續着這個自我完善的過程——我們希望父親醒來之後能夠以我們爲榮。

此時，夏·圖爾人出現了。
]], "_t")
t("history of Mal'Rok (2)", "瑪·洛克的歷史（2）", "_t")
t([[They arrived in enormous flying fortresses, bristling with weapons and overflowing with magic. They did not directly threaten us, but they met with our leaders and gave us what was either an offer or an ultimatum: let them kill our Father, or kill him ourselves, and be rewarded with technology and magic as grand as theirs.

They were powerful - very powerful. Although their proposal was phrased as a generous offer, we could not help but notice that their fortresses had positioned themselves over our armories and population centers, and none of their fortresses were unarmed. We did not think we could fight them; we considered waking Father for help, but we weren't sure he could fight them either. In desperation, we met and devised a plan: we would seal Urh'Rok away, prevent him from waking up unless disturbed, and then tell the Sher'Tul what we had done. Father would not be hurt or injured by this - he simply wouldn't know what was going on.

We did this, and came to the Sher'Tul. They begrudgingly accepted our treacherous act as a pledge of loyalty to them, and came through with their end of the bargain, giving us knowledge and artifacts beyond our wildest dreams. They built powerful portals all over our planet, allowing us to travel through them not only within our world, but within every world the Sher'Tul had visited before. We saw wonderful new worlds, met and traded with peaceful species from across the universe, enjoyed all kinds of new, alien food, music, magic, and inventions, and generally could not have been happier with how things turned out - if not for the pangs of guilt we felt for betraying our Father. The Sher'Tul eventually stopped visiting us, but we kept trading with new people we met through the portal, and did not notice their absence.

Then everything broke.
]], [[他們乘着巨大的飛行堡壘前來，上面裝滿了各種武器，即使在遠處也可以感受到它放射出來的強大魔法力量。他們沒有直接威脅我們，但是他們和我們的領袖會面，像我們提出了一個交易——同時也是一個最後通牒：他們將動手殺掉父親，或者選擇我們自己動手幹掉他，這樣他們將會贈予給我們他們所有用的科技和魔法。

他們很強大——十分強大。儘管他們的交易看上去是一個慷慨的贈予，我們也情不自禁地發現，他們的堡壘全都全副武裝，所有的武器系統都瞄準了我們的兵工廠和人口中心。我們覺得我們無法擊敗他們；我們曾想過叫醒父親來幫助我們，但是我們害怕即使是父親或許也無法擊敗他們。在絕望之中，我們最終確定了一個計劃：我們將會把烏魯洛克封印起來，讓他除非被強大的力量打擾否則不會醒來，並告訴夏·圖爾人我們所做的事。父親不會被這樣的封印所傷害——他甚至不知道之後發生了什麼。

我們做了這些，並且告知了夏·圖爾人。他們勉強同意把我們背叛的行爲當作是對他們忠誠的象徵，按照約定，他們給了我們許多的知識和充滿奧術力量的神器——這些東西超越了我們最狂野的夢想。他們在我們星球的各處建造了強大的傳送門，讓我們不僅可以在我們的星球隨處穿行，還可以到達夏·圖爾人所訪問過的任何一個地方。我們看到了美好的新世界，與宇宙各處友好的生物互相會面，互相交易，享受來自各個星球的食物、音樂、魔法和各種發明。這幾乎是我們最快樂的日子——如果不是我們心中還壞着背叛父親的深深愧疚之情的話。夏·圖爾人最終停止了對我們的訪問，但我們仍然繼續着利用傳送門和其他地方的人聯絡交易，並沒有注意到它們突然消失了。

然而，就在此時，美好的生活突然破碎了。
]], "_t")
t("history of Mal'Rok (3)", "瑪·洛克的歷史（3）", "_t")
t([[Waves of terrible magic burst forth from the portals, which it's now clear were never intended to help us. They were a deadly trap, a ticking time bomb that would go off when the Sher'Tul wanted it to - and it went off with incredible force. Most of the worlds we had once visited were obliterated completely. Ours was not, but I can barely say we were "spared"; our Father's jungles turned to a cursed pyre instantly, burning with flame that could never be extinguished, and our planet cracked apart, whole continents flying into the void. What little land was left obviously couldn't be used for farming. Most of us died instantly, the survivors being those close enough to a skilled mage who could create enough oxygen to breathe, and convert ambient magic into caloric energy for our bodies. Life for the survivors was - is - endless torment, the burning ground constantly searing our feet, and all the beauty we once knew destroyed.

Fortunately, this woke our Father up. We confessed our treachery, but did not beg forgiveness, as we knew what we had done was unforgivable; he disagreed, and to this day is using nearly every shred of his power to keep the shattered fragments of our planet together. We were not satisfied with this fate, our Father suffering and exhausting himself for the sake of our mistakes. We begged him to give us a command, something we could do to help his situation, or at least make him happier about it.

His command: End the Sher'Tul. End their creations. Never let anything be hurt by Eyal again.

We have taken his words to heart. Our mages have devised new magic from old inspiration, alteration spells to make us warlike and brutal once more - but with our ascended minds and honed bodies, we shall be a force of destruction far greater than the dust-storms ever were. Our green bretheren underwent a process to make their skin drip with acid; not to be outdone, our onyx brethren grew faster and stronger, with a birth-rate high enough to overwhelm whatever Sher'Tul or Sher'Tul-made monsters lay on Eyal. The red ones proclaimed they now existed only to destroy, and fused bits of the burnt earth to their hands, leaving them unable to do anything but sear Eyal with its own fires. The finished results of these alterations have taken up residence on our largest drifting continent, the one drawing ever closer to Eyal.

Once this continent arrives, we shall take revenge on Eyal. Not just for our own sakes, our planet ravaged by their treachery, with a pristine one waiting as our prize. Not just for our Father's sake, condemned to an eternity of suffering for trusting his children too much. But for *everyone's* sake, the untold trillions of souls on planets less fortunate than ours, torn apart in a fiery instant. The Sher'Tul shall never hurt anyone again; we shall make sure of it by cleansing Eyal in blighted fire, and any survivors will be taken back to our planet and chained to the burning earth, kept alive so they can forever feel the flames they created consuming their flesh. Their eternal torture will still not be justice, as they shall feel only a tiny portion of the suffering they inflicted... but it's a start.
]], [[很顯然，夏·圖爾人從來沒有真心想要過幫助我們。在那一天，一股可怕的破壞性魔法能量從所有的傳送門中放射出來。這一切都是他們設置的死亡陷阱，這些傳送門都是具有強大力量的定時炸彈，只要夏·圖爾人想要就會隨時爆炸。大部分我們曾經訪問過的世界幾乎被瞬間湮滅。我們的世界仍然殘存，但是被強大的爆炸力量炸了個粉碎：我們父親創造的叢林被魔法能量的詛咒下瞬間變成了沖天的永恆火柱，燃燒的火焰永遠無法被任何方法撲滅，我們的星球被炸裂開來，大部分的大陸都被消失在無盡的虛空之中。即使是殘留下來的少許土地，也永遠無法用於耕種。我們中的大部分人當場死亡，剩下來極其少數的強大法師試着用魔法創造了用於呼吸的氧氣，將周圍涌動的魔法能量轉化成我們身體所需要的能量。對於那些倖存者來說，生命宛如無盡的折磨，燃燒的大地在我們的腳下灼燒，我們曾見過的一切美好事物都被焚燬殆盡。

幸運的是，這場天災地變驚醒了我們的父親。我們爲我們背叛的行爲深深懺悔，然而我們不是爲了乞求原諒，因爲我們所做的一切永遠沒法被原諒。他並不同意，使用了他全部的力量將我們破碎的星球重新維持在了一起。我們對這樣不公命運感到十分痛心，我們的父親因爲我們的錯誤不得不而竭盡全力受盡磨難，卻仍然決意爲我們付出。我們向他祈求，希望他向我們下達命令。我們願意做任何我們能做的來幫助他，至少能夠讓他感到喜悅。

他的命令是：終結夏·圖爾人。終結他們的造物。讓埃亞爾的住民再也無法危害人間。

我們將他的話銘記在心。我們的法師從過去被我們廢棄的法術中獲取靈感，創造了新的法術，讓我們再一次變得好戰和殘忍——然而，我們的意志早已變得更加堅定，我們的身體早已鍛鍊得更加強韌，我們將會成爲毀滅一切的力量——比那些過去的塵土風暴更加可怕。我們綠翡翠色的同胞讓他們的皮膚上滴落酸液，縞瑪瑙之子也不甘示弱，強化自己的身體，讓自己更高、更快、更強。紅寶石之子更是聲稱他們唯一存在的意義就是爲了毀滅一切，他們將我們星球上永久灼燒的土地融合在他們的手上，失去雙手的他們無法做任何事情，畢生的精力都將用於以他們的烈火將埃亞爾的一切燃燒殆盡。我們的生育率也大大提高，遠遠超過了埃亞爾上的夏·圖爾人和他們創造的一切怪物。最終，這些變化了自身的同胞在我們星球飄逸在外的最大碎片上定居，操縱着碎片在埃亞爾的上空盤旋。

當這塊大陸的碎片降臨埃亞爾，我們將開始我們真正的復仇。那不僅僅是爲了我們自己的原因：我們的星球被他們的背信棄義所蹂躪，只有將它們的自己完好無損的星球作爲戰利品才能補償我們的損失。那不僅僅是爲了我們父親的原因：因爲太過信任自己的孩子，他遭受了這樣永恆的磨難和苦痛。那是爲了世界上的所有人：那些在無數星球上受苦受難的億萬生靈，他們沒有像我們那樣的幸運，在災難中瞬間被烈火吞噬。夏·圖爾人再也不能這樣爲害人間，我們將用枯萎之火淨化整個埃亞爾。任何殘存的生還者將會被帶到我們的星球，綁在無盡灼燒的土地上經受永恆的折磨，讓他們體會自己所造下的罪孽和折磨降臨到自己身上的感覺。即使這樣也不足以彌補它們所做的惡行，他們所將經歷的只是他們所造成的邪惡的一小部分……但是這將是一個開始。
]], "_t")
t("Lost Memories (1)", "遺失的記憶（1）", "_t")
t([[#{italic}#You clutch your head.  Entering this next floor, memories of your imprisonment flood back to you...#{normal}#

"All right, bring in the next one," says the ruby-skinned leader.  A few small, green and black things mop up the pile of muck that used to be a dwarf, and you move to the front of the line and stand where he used to be.  On the other side of the room, another <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?> stands on an identical platform.  This is exciting - you've been specially chosen as a test subject!  You hope you help them find something effective AND agonizing, and look forward to the pain to come.  A green imp, a little more mutated and knobbly than the rest you've seen, stands on your side of the room and grins at you with anticipation;  on the other side, a more normal imp approaches your counterpart.  "Control group...  go."  The normal wretchling leaps on the <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?>'s face, clutching it tight as a torrent of acid oozes from its skin, then lets go; the red imp looks at his melting flesh, jots down some notes, then mutters "and pain blocks off..."  The <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?>'s smile vanishes, and he clutches his face, then lets out a howling scream, collapses, and begins writhing on the floor.  The red imp looks down again, gives a bored sigh, and takes some more notes.  "That's enough, pain blocks on, patch him up."  The <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?> stops moving, stands up, and smiles again, the acid continuing to eat away at his flesh until a pipe in the floor douses him with some sort of chemical.  Another red imp mutters something and waves his hands before taking his hand and leading him off, and you see his horrible wounds gradually healing.

"Experimental group...  go."  With speed you can't even process until it's already on you, the mutant wretchling leaps onto your face.  You feel no pain as its acid leaks over your torso, although you do feel an odd sensation of your skin layers beginning to dissolve.  The imp leaps off again; apparently it missed your eyes, because you can see the red imp looking somewhat disappointed.  "Structural damage subpar...  okay, pain blocks off."  You know you're not supposed to scream during this next part.

You scream.  You scream harder than you have in your life, to the point where you think you might be tearing your vocal cords apart.  The pain is stronger not just than any pain you've ever felt, but any sensation you've ever felt.  You fall to the ground and claw at your skin, tearing off bits of it as you try to get the acid off.  You struggle and flail, instinctively grabbing at anything that could help you even though you know there's nothing in reach that could.

"All right, nice!  Pain blocks on!"  And just like that, the pain vanishes; your skin still bubbles, but that horrible pain is gone, and even your throat isn't sore.  "Clean him and patch him up.  Pain-amplifying qualities...  significant improvement...  recommend breeding with low-pain high-corrosion specimens."  A shower of unidentifiable goo washes over you, and your skin stops bubbling; your handler takes your arm and leads you away, muttering a healing spell under his breath, and your scars slowly start to fade into smooth skin once again.  You hope they aren't too harsh on you for screaming, but the way that imp spoke...  you must've helped them learn something!  You grin from ear to ear as you leave the room, hearing the red imp yell "Next!" as the door closes behind you.

#{italic}#You shudder.#{normal}#
]], [[#{italic}#你緊緊地抱住自己的頭，一踏入下一層，被囚禁的記憶如潮水般涌來……#{normal}#

"很好，下一個。"紅寶石色皮膚的指揮道。一小羣矮小的、黑綠的東西擦乾了曾是<?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?>的灰燼，你走到隊首，站在<?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?>剛纔的位置。在房間的另一邊，另一個同族站在同樣的平臺上。這讓你有些激動——你被選中爲實驗對象！你希望你能對他們的研究有所助益，希望能找到更加有效、更加“痛苦”的方法，同時期望着痛苦的降臨。一隻綠色的小惡魔——形態似乎有些變異，比你通常見到的骨節更加突出——站在你身邊，充滿期待地微笑着。另一邊，一隻較爲正常的小惡魔走向你的夥伴。“控制組準備……開始”那隻正常的酸液樹魔踩在他臉上，緊緊地按住，同時一股酸液從皮膚中涌出。紅色的小惡魔看了看他融化的肉體，略記了些什麼，然後小聲說道“痛苦阻斷關閉……”他臉上的笑容突然消失了，他抓着自己的臉，然後發出痛苦地哀嚎，倒在地上，不停翻滾着。紅色小惡魔再次低下頭看了看，厭倦地嘆了口氣，繼續寫着。“好吧，痛苦阻斷打開，把他帶走。”他停止了翻滾，站了起來，再度微笑，酸液繼續吞噬着他的血肉，直到房間裏的管子朝他噴灑了藥劑。另一隻紅色小惡魔咕噥了幾句，擺擺手，帶着他離開了。同時，你看見他身上可怕的傷害漸漸癒合。

“實驗組……開始”你還沒反應過來，那隻變異的酸液樹魔已經踩在你臉上了。當酸液滴落在你軀幹上時，你並沒有感到疼痛，只有一種古怪的皮膚消融的感覺。小惡魔再次低頭向下看；顯然他漏看了你的眼睛，因爲你能看到他神色中的失望。“結構傷害……好的，痛苦阻斷解除”你認爲下一步驟裏大家都期望着你不會發出尖叫。

你尖叫着，痛苦地尖叫着，發出你一生從未有過的哀嚎，你甚至以爲自己的聲帶將被撕裂。這痛苦比以往的任何痛苦更加強烈，比任何感覺都要強烈。你跌倒在地，用手抓撓着皮膚，希望將酸液除去。你掙扎着，抓撓着，攥住手邊任何東西，希望能解除痛苦，儘管你心裏清楚這並不可能。

“很好，非常好！痛苦阻斷打開！”剛聽到這裏，剛纔的痛苦頓時消失了；你的皮膚仍在顫抖，但痛苦不再，甚至喉嚨也不疼了。“洗乾淨，帶下去。痛苦加倍……重要改進……建議同低痛高腐蝕型雜交。”一股不知名的液體朝你噴射，你的皮膚不再溶解。你的“主人”抓住你的胳膊，帶着你離開，同時向你釋放治療法術。你的傷痕消褪了。你希望他們不會因爲你的尖叫而對你加以懲處，不過，從你聽到的隻言片語，你應該對他們有所幫助。想到這裏，你不禁咧嘴笑了，身後的門關閉時，迴響着那隻小惡魔叫喊“下一個”的聲音。

#{italic}#你不禁打了個寒顫。#{normal}#
]], "_t")
t("Lost Memories (2)", "遺失的記憶（2）", "_t")
t([[#{italic}#More memories rush into your mind...#{normal}#

"It's your lucky day, <?=player.name?>," your handler says as he leads you to a large, glowing crystal.  "You're too cooperative to stay in testing any longer.  Today, you're getting promoted to research assistant!"  You're nearly beside yourself with joy!  "Now, we'll need to do a short little process first.  Fireproofing wards here, loyalty reinforcement there, standard-issue alteration, but mostly just linking your consciousness to this," he says, pointing to the crystal.  "With this thing, everything you see, hear, smell, taste, or feel gets fed directly into this little ol' beauty.  Not just that, either - whereever you go, and whatever you think, we'll have it saved for future reference."  You're going to help them learn so much!  "Just step on the plate here, and hold your arms like this so I can get the bindings in place..."

That crystal.  That crystal is how they're keeping track of you, and it has most of what you helped them discover trapped within it.  If you break it, you'll be able to escape their notice for the first time since you arrived here, allowing you to get away without them finding you again, and as an added bonus you'll undo most of what you helped them accomplish.  You need to destroy it, then flee for your life!]], [[#{italic}#更多記憶涌入了你的腦海……#{normal}#

“記住，這是你的幸運日，”你的“主人”帶着你到一塊巨大的閃耀水晶面前，“你非常合作，因此你將從一般實驗中解放。現在你被提升爲研究助理！”聞言，你欣喜若狂！“好了，現在我們需要先做一些事情。火焰防護在這，忠誠強化在那，標準化思維修改，呃，不過主要還是將你的意識鏈接到這裏，”他一邊說，一邊指着水晶體,“有了這個，你看到的、聽到的、嗅到的、嚐到的、感覺到的全都能體現在這塊美麗精巧的水晶裏。不僅如此，不管你去哪，不管你想什麼，都能記錄下來，以供研究。”你突然發現自己能幫助他們研究如此之多！“站在那裏別動，舉起胳膊，這樣我就能把它放好……”

那塊水晶，對，那就是他們追蹤你的方式，同時也記載了他們對你的大部分研究。如果你摧毀了它，你就能避開他們的注意，逃出這裏，不被他們發現。同時，還能毀了他們的部分研究成果。你必須要摧毀它，然後逃跑！
]], "_t")
t("orbital base: battle plan (doombringer)", "軌道基地: 戰鬥計劃（毀滅使者）", "_t")
t([[Engagement Briefing on <?=player.name?>:

This slippery little <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?> has proven to be a thorn in our side so far.  We've reinforced our wards to better protect against the sort of fluke meteor impact that enabled <?=player:his_her()?> escape, but the crystal <?=player:he_she()?> smashed on <?=player:his_her()?> way out prevented us from keeping track of <?=player:his_her()?> location directly.  No matter - the brands and marks we've imbued <?=player:him_her()?> with have nonetheless allowed us to monitor magical energy signals affecting <?=player:him_her()?>, and our scryers have noted that there appears to be a particular pattern that teleports <?=player:him_her()?>, possibly of Sher'Tul origin.  We've sent out a signal of our own to intercept this, and redirect it to our platform, where <?=player:he_she()?> will be safely secured, punished for <?=player:his_her()?> disobedience, then once again exposed to a Tablet of Enlightenment to regain <?=player:his_her()?> servitude.

That said, given that <?=player:he_she()?> has increased dramatically in power since <?=player:his_her()?> escape, it is crucial that we keep proper tactics in mind.  Having been exposed to our alteration magic, <?=player:he_she()?> is very formidable in direct melee combat, and in the event that we cannot procure proper warding against this magic before <?=player:his_her()?> arrival, <?=player:he_she()?> can cause significant damage if not properly handled.  Under no circumstances should we let <?=player:him_her()?> run rampant in our back line; furthermore, if we simply try to lure <?=player:him_her()?> into a narrow corridor, we will not be able to bring enough firepower to bear before <?=player:he_she()?> can break through our obstructions.  Instead, use a small flanking squad backed up by a maulotaur (or whatever high-power direct combatant we can get authorization to deploy) to force <?=player:him_her()?> into an open area, where we'll have caster artillery, protected by a front-line of wretchlings backed by quasits.  We may lose these front-line soldiers, but in the time it takes <?=player:him_her()?> to slash <?=player:his_her()?> way through them, our spells should be able to reduce <?=player:him_her()?> to a flayed, quivering wreck.

Above all else, remember: despite <?=player:his_her()?> brute strength, this is a pitiful, inferior Eyalite who lucked <?=player:his_her()?> way into obtaining some of our superior power.  <?=player:he_she():capitalize()?> does not know how to use it properly, and does not have the countless years of experience with it that we do.  We have numbers, familiarity, tactics, and the blessing of Urh'Rok himself.  Treat this like a drill; if we stay calm and focused, it is unlikely we will see any casualties.
]], [[有關<?=player.name?>的戰術簡報：

這個該死的小 <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?> 目前是我們的眼中釘、肉中刺。我們已經加強了我們的防禦，避免在發生類似於隕石衝擊導致像<?=player:his_her()?>這樣的犯人逃跑這樣的意外。然而，由於<?=player:he_she()?>在<?=player:his_her()?>逃跑路上砸壞了水晶，我們無法直接跟蹤到<?=player:his_her()?>當前的位置。不過這不要緊——儘管如此，我們在<?=player:him_her()?>的身上注入的魔法痕跡仍然讓我們可以偵測到<?=player:him_her()?>身上的魔法能量信號。我們的占卜師已經發現<?=player:him_her()?>在使用某種特定的魔法傳送自己——似乎是某種夏·圖爾人的發明。我們發出了干擾的魔法信號，將傳送落點重定向到我們的平臺。在那裏，<?=player:he_she()?>可以被“安全”地保護起來，懲罰<?=player:him_her()?>違抗命令的舉動，並使用我們的啓蒙石板來恢復<?=player:his_her()?>忠誠。

這就是說，由於<?=player:he_she()?>的實力從<?=player:his_her()?>上一次逃跑開始計算已經大幅增長，把明確的戰略戰術銘記在心對我們來說是極爲重要的。長期曝露在我們的改良魔法之下，<?=player:he_she()?>在近戰格鬥中表現令人生畏。如果我們在<?=player:he_she()?>到來前妥善組織防禦對抗他的魔法，<?=player:he_she()?>可能會對我們的部隊造成極大的損傷。我們在任何情況下都絕不能讓<?=player:him_her()?>擊穿我們部隊的後防線；也就是說，如果我們僅僅是把<?=player:him_her()?>引誘到一個狹窄的角落，我們的火力或許沒有辦法阻止他衝破重圍。正確的方法應當是，先用一支由瑪諾陶（或者其他任何我們能夠調動的高階近戰部隊）帶領的佯攻小隊將<?=player:him_her()?>引誘到空曠地帶，然後讓我們的法師部隊在前線酸液樹魔和誇塞魔的掩護下發動攻擊。我們可能會損失大量的前線部隊，但是這可以有效阻攔<?=player:him_her()?>前進的腳步。在此期間，我們的法術力量足以將他打成馬蜂窩。

最重要的是：請記住，儘管<?=player:his_her()?>有一身蠻力，<?=player:he_she()?>只是一個可憐的，下等的埃亞爾人，只是出於幸運纔有機會竊取了我們惡魔的強大力量。<?=player:he_she()?>並不真正瞭解如何正確使用自己的能力，也不像我們那樣有着長期豐富的作戰經驗。我們有數量優勢、有團結精神、有戰術協作、還有烏魯洛克大人的祝福。像對待演習一樣對待這場戰鬥，只要保持審慎和專注，我們不會受到什麼損失。
]], "_t")
t("orbital base: battle plan (demonologist)", "軌道基地: 戰鬥計劃（惡魔使者）", "_t")
t([[Engagement Briefing on <?=player.name?>:

This slippery little <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?> has proven to be a thorn in our side so far.  We've reinforced our wards to better protect against the sort of fluke meteor impact that enabled <?=player:his_her()?> escape, but the crystal <?=player:he_she()?> smashed on <?=player:his_her()?> way out prevented us from keeping track of <?=player:his_her()?> location directly.  No matter - the brands and marks we've imbued <?=player:him_her()?> with have nonetheless allowed us to monitor magical energy signals affecting <?=player:him_her()?>, and our scryers have noted that there appears to be a particular pattern that teleports <?=player:him_her()?>, possibly of Sher'Tul origin.  We've sent out a signal of our own to intercept this, and redirect it to our platform, where <?=player:he_she()?> will be safely secured, punished for <?=player:his_her()?> disobedience, then once again exposed to a Tablet of Enlightenment to regain <?=player:his_her()?> servitude.

That said, given that <?=player:he_she()?> has increased dramatically in power since <?=player:his_her()?> escape, it is crucial that we keep proper tactics in mind.  We've heard disturbing reports that some of our species have been spotted fighting alongside <?=player:him_her()?>; we can assume that <?=player:he_she()?> is using a twisted version of the Tablet's power to enslave some of our forces.  Much of <?=player:his_her()?> combat potential comes from these thralls, rather than <?=player:his_her()?> own abilities.  Accordingly, there are three things to keep in mind:

-Prioritize the Eyalite, rather than <?=player:his_her()?> thralls.  We do not yet have a concrete understanding of how <?=player:he_she()?> is controlling our allies, but it seems likely that the mental hold will break once <?=player:he_she()?>'s incapacitated; if <?=player:he_she()?> has managed to take control of a Champion of Urh'Rok or similarly powerful agent, we should focus our firepower on <?=player:him_her()?> instead.  That said, neutralizing <?=player:him_her()?> is more important than saving the time and effort of producing such a creature; in particular, don't worry about catching a few enthralled imps in the crossfire.  No matter what <?=player:he_she()?>'s using, we can make more of it.

-Be ready for anything.  We've never needed to plan out what to do against our own powers, and we have such a diverse set of species that <?=player:he_she()?> could throw all kinds of magic or martial prowess against us.  This might sound hopeless, but remember: you've seen all this in action before, these powers being used alongside yours in training and in combat.  Whatever you've seen your comrades do, expect to see it from <?=player:him_her()?>.

-Do not assume that the onslaught will stop if all of <?=player:his_her()?> thralls are dead.  <?=player:he_she():capitalize()?> has managed to directly imbue <?=player:his_her_self()?> with some of our magic, and may be capable of using our fireballs, acidic bursts, and so forth.  Silencing magic will be helpful here, as will spells that can drain <?=player:his_her()?> energy; furthermore, ripping away <?=player:his_her()?> shield will make <?=player:him_her()?> especially vulnerable to our claws and axes.

Above all else, remember: despite <?=player:his_her()?> enthralled minions, this is a pitiful, inferior Eyalite who lucked <?=player:his_her()?> way into obtaining some of our superior power.  <?=player:he_she():capitalize()?> does not know how to use it properly, and does not have the countless years of experience with it that we do.  We have numbers, familiarity, tactics, and the blessing of Urh'Rok himself.  Treat this like a drill; if we stay calm and focused, it is unlikely we will see any casualties.
]], [[有關<?=player.name?>的戰術簡報：

這個該死的小 <?=_t(player.descriptor.subrace, "birth descriptor name")?> 目前是我們的眼中釘、肉中刺。我們已經加強了我們的防禦，避免在發生類似於隕石衝擊導致像<?=player:his_her()?>這樣的犯人逃跑這樣的意外。然而，由於<?=player:he_she()?>在<?=player:his_her()?>逃跑路上砸壞了水晶，我們無法直接跟蹤到<?=player:his_her()?>當前的位置。不過這不要緊——儘管如此，我們在<?=player:him_her()?>的身上注入的魔法痕跡仍然讓我們可以偵測到<?=player:him_her()?>身上的魔法能量信號。我們的占卜師已經發現<?=player:him_her()?>在使用某種特定的魔法傳送自己——似乎是某種夏·圖爾人的發明。我們發出了干擾的魔法信號，將傳送落點重定向到我們的平臺。在那裏，<?=player:he_she()?>可以被“安全”地保護起來，懲罰<?=player:him_her()?>違抗命令的舉動，並使用我們的啓蒙石板來恢復<?=player:his_her()?>忠誠。

這就是說，由於<?=player:he_she()?>的實力從<?=player:his_her()?>上一次逃跑開始計算已經大幅增長，把明確的戰略戰術銘記在心對我們來說是極爲重要的。我們收到了一些令人不安的消息，據說有人目擊到一些我們的同族和<?=player:him_her()?>一起戰鬥；我們猜測，<?=player:he_she()?>一定是使用了某種和石板的力量類似的方法來奴役了我們的一些部隊。顯然，<?=player:his_her()?>大部分的戰鬥能力來自其所操縱的惡魔的力量，而不是<?=player:his_her()?>自己的能力。因此，有三件事情我們必須始終銘記在心。

—集中火力對付那個埃亞爾人，而不是那些被<?=player:he_she()?>奴役的惡魔。我們目前尚不能準確地瞭解到底<?=player:he_she()?>是怎麼控制那些惡魔的，不過顯然，只要擊敗<?=player:he_she()?>那些精神枷鎖就會立刻解除。如果<?=player:he_she()?>不知怎麼地召喚出了烏魯洛克的精英衛兵這樣的強力惡魔，我們必須把火力集中在<?=player:him_her()?>本人身上。從另外一方面來說，將<?=player:him_her()?>徹底消滅比製造惡魔的時間和精力要重要得多。因此，不用擔心走火意外擊中<?=player:he_she()?>所奴役的幾隻小酸液樹魔這樣的事情而擔心太多。無論<?=player:he_she()?>手中有多少惡魔，我們的戰爭機器永遠能夠製造更多。

—準備好面對任何困難的處境。我們從來沒有做過與我們的同族作戰的準備，並且由於我們的族類十分豐富，<?=player:he_she()?>可以施展各種各樣的魔法和戰爭技巧來對付我們。這聽上去似乎有點絕望，不過，請記住：無論怎樣，<?=player:he_she()?>所施展的技能你之前都曾經親身經歷過，他的能力都是你在鍛鍊和戰鬥中所見過的能力。只要想想你的同志們曾經使用過什麼技能，你就能想到<?=player:him_her()?>將會使用的技能了。

—不要在擊敗了所有被奴役的惡魔之後就對<?=player:his_her()?>掉以輕心，似乎<?=player:he_she()?>已經掌握了某種把惡魔的力量和<?=player:his_her_self()?>結合的方法，足以釋放近戰火球，酸性爆發等一系列技能。一定要及時對其釋放沉默魔法，或者任何可以吸乾<?=player:his_her()?>的生命能量的方法。另外，用繳械技能卸下<?=player:his_her()?>的盾牌，<?=player:him_her()?>在我們的刀槍劍斧面前就會顯得無比脆弱。

最重要的是：請記住，儘管<?=player:his_her()?>不知怎麼奴役了我們的一些同類，<?=player:he_she()?>只是一個可憐的，下等的埃亞爾人，只是出於幸運纔有機會竊取了我們惡魔的強大力量。<?=player:he_she()?>並不真正瞭解如何正確使用自己的能力，也不像我們那樣有着長期豐富的作戰經驗。我們有數量優勢、有團結精神、有戰術協作、還有烏魯洛克大人的祝福。像對待演習一樣對待這場戰鬥，只要保持審慎和專注，我們不會受到什麼損失。
]], "_t")
t("orbital base: battle plan (doomelf)", "軌道基地: 戰鬥計劃（魔化精靈）", "_t")
t([[Engagement Briefing on <?=player.name?>:

This slippery little elf has proven to be a thorn in our side so far.  We've reinforced our wards to better protect against the sort of fluke meteor impact that enabled <?=player:his_her()?> escape, but the crystal <?=player:he_she()?> smashed on <?=player:his_her()?> way out prevented us from keeping track of <?=player:his_her()?> location directly.  No matter - the brands and marks we've imbued <?=player:him_her()?> with have nonetheless allowed us to monitor magical energy signals affecting <?=player:him_her()?>, and our scryers have noted that there appears to be a particular pattern that teleports <?=player:him_her()?>, possibly of Sher'Tul origin.  We've sent out a signal of our own to intercept this, and redirect it to our platform, where <?=player:he_she()?> will be safely secured, punished for <?=player:his_her()?> disobedience, then once again exposed to a Tablet of Enlightenment to regain <?=player:his_her()?> servitude.

That said, given that <?=player:he_she()?> has increased dramatically in power since <?=player:his_her()?> escape, it is crucial that we keep proper tactics in mind.  Our standard alterations have synergized with this Shalore's natural reactive magic, giving <?=player:him_her()?> short-range teleportation to rival Draebor and creating a frustratingly evasive target to hit.  Even <?=player:his_her()?> internal organs are affected, and will slide out of the way in anticipation of a blow that would strike an otherwise-vital area.  Compared to standard Shalore, <?=player:he_she()?> cannot directly turn invisible, but seems to have adopted a form of dúathedlen magic to remain out of sight all the same; if the requisition order for light-based wards goes through, this and the blasts of darkness this form grants should both be a non-issue.  Finally, use of more advanced combat maneuvers will be somewhat impeded by <?=player:his_her()?> ability to interfere with our concentration, and the resilience alterations we gave <?=player:him_her()?> will make <?=player:him_her()?> shrug off poisons, flames, and the like much quicker than usual.

What does all this mean?  Just get <?=player:him_her()?> wounded, wait for <?=player:him_her()?> to try to teleport away, then get <?=player:him_her()?> in a corner and beat <?=player:him_her()?> until <?=player:he_she()?> stops moving.  It's really that simple.  Just work that into our standard methods of dealing with <?=string.a_an(_t(player.descriptor.subclass, "birth descriptor name"):lower())?>, remember not to break ranks if <?=player:he_she()?> vanishes into darkness, and we'll have this mess cleaned up in no time.

Above all else, remember: despite <?=player:his_her()?> enhancements, this is a pitiful, inferior Eyalite who lucked <?=player:his_her()?> way into obtaining some of our superior power.  <?=player:he_she():capitalize()?> does not know how to use it properly, and does not have the countless years of experience with it that we do.  We have numbers, familiarity, tactics, and the blessing of Urh'Rok himself.  Treat this like a drill; if we stay calm and focused, it is unlikely we will see any casualties.

]], [[有關<?=player.name?>的戰術簡報：

這個該死的小精靈目前是我們的眼中釘、肉中刺。我們已經加強了我們的防禦，避免在發生類似於隕石衝擊導致像<?=player:his_her()?>這樣的犯人逃跑這樣的意外。然而，由於<?=player:he_she()?>在<?=player:his_her()?>逃跑路上砸壞了水晶，我們無法直接跟蹤到<?=player:his_her()?>當前的位置。不過這不要緊——儘管如此，我們在<?=player:him_her()?>的身上注入的魔法痕跡仍然讓我們可以偵測到<?=player:him_her()?>身上的魔法能量信號。我們的占卜師已經發現<?=player:him_her()?>在使用某種特定的魔法傳送自己——似乎是某種夏·圖爾人的發明。我們發出了干擾的魔法信號，將傳送落點重定向到我們的平臺。在那裏，<?=player:he_she()?>可以被“安全”地保護起來，懲罰<?=player:him_her()?>違抗命令的舉動，並使用我們的啓蒙石板來恢復<?=player:his_her()?>忠誠。

這就是說，由於<?=player:he_she()?>的實力從<?=player:his_her()?>上一次逃跑開始計算已經大幅增長，把明確的戰略戰術銘記在心對我們來說是極爲重要的。我們調整了永恆精靈天賦的加速能力，讓<?=player:him_her()?>可以像小惡魔德瑞寶那樣使用短距離傳送技能，並在傳送後大幅提升閃避能力。就連<?=player:his_her()?>內部器官也受到了影響，使其可以自動把一些瞄準要害的攻擊轉移到其他並不那麼重要的地方。與普通的永恆精靈相比，<?=player:he_she()?>並不能直接隱身，但似乎採取了轉化成多瑟頓的方式來隱藏自己。即使有人使用照明的方式尋找到了<?=player:him_her()?>的位置，也可以使用多瑟頓製造暗影爆炸的能力來解決問題。此外，<?=player:he_she()?>可以集中精力衝擊對方的精神來打斷對方的高級戰鬥策略，並且在惡魔空間的試煉增強了<?=player:his_her()?>的韌性，使其可以快速擺脫異常狀態。

這意味着什麼？很顯然，只需要先擊傷<?=player:him_her()?>，等着<?=player:him_her()?>自己選擇傳送逃跑，然後乘勝追擊將<?=player:him_her()?>堵在狹小的角落發動集中攻擊直到其放棄移動。就是這麼簡單，接下來只要考慮我們對付<?=_t(player.descriptor.subclass)?>的一般策略就可以了。記住，在<?=player:he_she()?>潛入黑暗的時候不要輕舉妄動，保持陣型，很快我們就能將其擊敗。

最重要的是：請記住，儘管<?=player:his_her()?>獲得了一些強化，<?=player:he_she()?>只是一個可憐的，下等的埃亞爾人，只是出於幸運纔有機會竊取了我們惡魔的強大力量。<?=player:he_she()?>並不真正瞭解如何正確使用自己的能力，也不像我們那樣有着長期豐富的作戰經驗。我們有數量優勢、有團結精神、有戰術協作、還有烏魯洛克大人的祝福。像對待演習一樣對待這場戰鬥，只要保持審慎和專注，我們不會受到什麼損失。
]], "_t")
t("orbital base: battle info", "軌道基地: 戰鬥情報", "_t")
t([[#{italic}#This note is splattered with the blood of the demon who was carrying it.#{normal}#

#{bold}#URGENT:#{normal}#

Operation to secure <?=player.name?> failure.  Primary defense force routed, secondary team taking heavy casualties.  All is lost.  Highest priority is now containing <?=player.name?> to prevent further damage.  Blow all connectors, break platform off the continent and dispel oxygenation wards befo--

#{italic}#The last O trails off, a line leading from it to the end of the page like the pen was rapidly jerked away.  You must have interrupted this demon's writing.#{normal}#
]], [[#{italic}#這張便條被攜帶他的惡魔的血弄髒了。#{normal}#

#{bold}#緊急事項：#{normal}#

對 <?=player.name?> 的保全監禁計劃失敗。主要防禦力量被擊退，應急部隊遭受嚴重損失。計劃完全失敗。正在啓動高優先級措施以防止 <?=player.name?> 造成進一步的損失。關閉所有鏈接傳送門，將所屬的平臺從大陸上分離，關閉氧氣生成設備，並——

#{italic}#最後一個字歪歪扭扭，一條墨水細線向下劃去直到頁面的底部，那是筆從手上滑落留下的痕跡。看來，你打斷了這個惡魔的書寫。#{normal}#
]], "_t")
t("orbital base: battle info with #{bold}#a badass#{normal}#", "軌道基地: 有關一個#{bold}#碉堡的人#的戰鬥情報{normal}#", "_t")
t([[#{italic}#This note is stained with what appear to be motorcycle tire-tracks.#{normal}#

#{bold}#URGENT:#{normal}#

Operation to secure <?=player.name?> failure.  Primary defense force routed by target's overwhelming badassery, secondary team presumed dead (reports inaudible over sound of face-melting guitar solos).  All is lost.  Totally worth it.  Highest priority is now isolating <?=player.name?>, building a stadium around <?=player:him_her()?>, and selling tickets to spectacle of badassery.  Blow all connectors, break platform off the continent, prepare pyrotechnics, and set up spotlights and speaker systems befo--

#{italic}#The last O trails off, a line leading from it to the end of the page like the pen was rapidly jerked away, then leads to a doodle depicting you, wielding a double-bladed katana and fighting a giant construct labelled "Ninja Atamathon."  Your badassery must have interrupted this demon's writing.#{normal}#
]], [[#{italic}#這張便條被摩托車輪胎的痕跡弄髒了。#{normal}#

#{bold}#緊急事項：#{normal}#

對 <?=player.name?> 的保全監禁計劃失敗。主要防禦力量被他的霸氣側漏嚇退，應急部隊推定已經死亡（報告的聲音被吉他獨奏的喧譁聲蓋住了）。雖然計劃完全失敗，但是這輩子值了。正在對 <?=player.name?> 啓動最高優先級措施，爲 <?=player:him_her()?> 建造一個體育場，讓觀衆買票入場觀看其霸氣側漏的情景。  關閉所有鏈接傳送門，將所屬的平臺從大陸上分離， 準備焰火，啓動閃光燈和音響系統並——

#{italic}#最後一個字歪歪扭扭，一條墨水細線向下劃去直到頁面的底部，那是筆從手上滑落留下的痕跡。下方是一幅關於你的塗鴉，手裏拿着武士刀，正在和“忍者王阿塔瑪森”對戰。看起來，你的霸氣側漏把這個惡魔嚇尿了。#{normal}#
]], "_t")
t("first mural painting", "第一幅壁畫", "_t")
t("#{italic}#\"To honor the Masters\" - A thrall#{normal}#", "#{italic}#“吾主萬歲”——您的奴僕#{normal}#", "_t")
t("second mural painting", "第二幅壁畫", "_t")
t("third mural painting", "第三幅壁畫", "_t")
t("fourth mural painting", "第四幅壁畫", "_t")
t("fifth mural painting", "第五幅壁畫", "_t")
t("sixth mural painting", "第六幅壁畫", "_t")
t("demon statue: wretchling", "惡魔雕像：酸液樹魔", "_t")
t("Behold, the humble wretchling, a testament to our devotion to our Father!  These children of emerald were among the first to alter themselves for our quest for vengeance, and managed an astounding degree of success.  With their bursts of blinding speed, overwhelming numbers, and skin that can release prodigious amounts of corrosive fluid, wretchlings can storm onto the battlefield and pounce on our foes one-by-one, dissolving the ground they walk on while leaving them helpless against our onslaught.  Wretchlings will readily give their lives in combat, serving as obstructions and shields while their acid and our casters do their work, and still remain the most populous of our species thanks to their incredible birth rates.  It is rare to see a wretchling survive to maturity, but make no mistake - every wretchling that fights does an incredible service to our cause.", [[看着他，謙遜的酸液樹魔，這是我們對父親奉獻一切的證明！這些綠翡翠的孩子們第一批同意改變自身以幫助復仇，同時取得了驚人的成功。極快的速度、龐大的數目以及能釋放大量酸液的皮膚，酸液樹魔能旋風般猛衝入戰場，一個個撲住敵人，溶解土地，將無助的敵人暴露在我們的殺戮前。酸液樹魔時刻準備着，懷着大無畏的犧牲精神，以肉體充當屏障，令酸液和法術能夠發揮作用。儘管如此，在他們驚人的繁殖率下，他們仍是我們中數目最多的種族。我們很難見到一隻酸液樹魔活到成熟期，但請記住——每一隻戰鬥過的酸液樹魔都爲我們的目標奉獻了一切。
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: fire imp", "惡魔雕像：火魔嬰", "_t")
t("If the Wretchling speaks to our worship, the Fire Imp speaks to our commitment and loyalty.  When a child of ruby goes out onto the battlefield, she fuses some of the Eyal-scarred earth from our planet to her hands, having perfected a type of magic that uses the raging magic contained within to blast our foes with the fires they've caused.  Aside from this means of appropriate justice being pleasing to Urh'Rok (as he showed when dealing with the dust-mages), it shows how dedicated we are to our cause: without hands, there's very little a Fire Imp would be able to do if she deserted or became demoralized.  Fighting and destroying is what we live for, and what better way to show it than making oneself unable to do anything but fight and destroy?  Although the bulk of the ruby species do not pursue this path, instead focusing on magical research and furthering our alteration projects, the example that the Fire Imp sets is a shining standard of commitment for all of Urh'Rok's children.", "如果說酸液樹魔證明了我們對父親的崇拜，那麼火魔嬰則證明了我們的忠誠。當紅寶石色的孩子來到戰場時，她將我們星球上被埃亞爾灼燒的土壤拿在手裏，完美運用一種特殊的狂暴魔法——使用敵人曾經傷害我們的火焰來消滅我們的敵人。除了展現恰如烏魯洛克之意的公正（正如他對塵埃法師們所做的一樣），這同樣體現了我們對目標的專注：沒有手的話，灰心喪氣的火魔嬰們通常什麼也幹不了，戰鬥和毀滅是我們的與生俱來的本性，除了讓一個生物只擁有殺戮和戰鬥的能力外，還有什麼能更好的表達這一點呢？儘管紅寶石的種族沒有沿着近身廝殺的道路走下去，他們以魔法的力量取而代之，火魔嬰們作爲我們的榜樣，爲我們——所有烏魯洛克的孩子們展現忠誠的標準。", "_t")
t("demon statue: water imp", "惡魔雕像：小水怪", "_t")
t("Though they retain use of their hands, this altered offshoot of the Fire Imp has made a much more powerful sacrifice: the ability to breathe air.  Most of the dominant species of Eyal reside above the water, making its oceans and lakes a prime location for carrying out covert operations, conducting experiments too dangerous to perform on our own soil, and preparing portals for a full-scale invasion.  As our scouts and servants beneath the seas, water imps forego the fire-slinging abilities shared by their brethren, instead focusing on ice-magic that is similarly effective underwater.  Like a wretchling, a Water Imp does not expect to live to see peacetime, and thus has no need to breathe above the surface.  Remember to pay tribute to the Water Imp whenever you can; since they do not fight alongside our land-based forces, it's all too easy to forget the selfless sacrifices they've made, and their enormous contributions in gathering intelligence and setting up remote bases.", [[儘管他們依舊使用雙手作戰，這羣變種的火魔嬰做出了更加偉大的犧牲：他們放棄了呼吸空氣的能力。大部分佔據主導地位的埃亞爾種族生活在水上，讓海洋和湖泊成爲我們的藏身的主要根據地，實施那些對於我們的土壤來說過於危險的實驗，同時爲製造全面侵略的傳送門做準備。作爲我們在海里的使者，小水怪們放棄了同胞們使用火焰的能力，轉而使用在水裏同樣有效的冰系法術。和酸液樹魔類似，小水怪們並不指望能活到和平到來，因此沒有必要在地表呼吸。請記得隨時爲小水怪們奉上禮物，不能因爲他們沒有同大家在地表作戰，就輕易遺忘他們做出的無私犧牲，以及爲彙集羣衆智慧、建立遠方基地做出的巨大貢獻。
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: quasit", "惡魔雕像：誇塞魔", "_t")
t("Clever and tough, the engineers and warriors of our kind, making armor for our forces and holding the front lines against the hordes of Eyal.  While the children of ruby study new magical spells for our arsenal, and the children of emerald study ways to make our own bodies deadlier, the children of onyx focus on making new constructs from scratch, lashing flesh, magic, and steel together into towering creations that strike fear into Eyal.  Those who fight on the front lines have been created to do so rather than born, churned out in a semi-mature state by factories with Forge-Giant-produced armor bolted onto their skin at \"birth.\"  Though they are mostly flesh, the warrior onyx known as Quasits are very much machines, made with bolstered muscles without losing the clever minds they come from.  As eager as they are brilliant, Quasits are well-disciplined and capable in combat, and their armor allows them to easily take blows that would devastate a Wretchling or Fire Imp.  Devotion will get us far on its own, but the Quasit shows how much more we can do when we have fervor and patience working hand-in-hand.", [[聰明而頑強，我們中的工程師與戰士，爲我們製造護甲，同時奮戰在埃亞爾邊界前線。紅寶石的孩子們學習兵工廠新的魔法，綠翡翠的孩子們學習令身軀更加致命的技巧，而瑪瑙色的孩子們專心學習新的構架體，將魔法、血肉和鋼鐵融爲一體，在埃亞爾大陸製造恐懼。那些奮戰在前線的，與其說是生出來，不如說是製造出來——在工廠裏由半成熟態大量炮製，一“出生”就身着鍛造巨人親制的護甲。儘管仍是血肉之軀，瑪瑙戰士——或者說誇塞魔——有着鋼鐵般的紀律和強大的近戰能力，同時他們的護甲能抵抗重擊，即使那重擊能輕易毀滅一隻酸液樹魔或者火魔嬰。奉獻讓我們向前邁進，但誇塞魔展示出，當我們擁有熱情和耐心攜手並進時，我們將走得更遠！
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: onilug", "惡魔雕像：歐尼路格", "_t")
t([[Necromancy. It has been a long practiced artform on our world, though it fell into disuse during the golden years of Urh'Rok. When the Sher'Tul annihilated our home, however, we resumed our studies on the use of this dark art.

Onilugs are Children of Onyx who have completely given themselves over to Death. The transformation process is both horrifying and painful, but the result is a demon fully tuned to manipulating necrotic energies. Their flesh has become dry and emaciated, making them appear as skeletal creatures draped in skin.  We salute those brave enough to undergo the transformation, for their work advances our cause of Eyal's destruction.

As they are no longer truly alive, onilugs do not fear the void of space. They may wander across the burnt landscape, not afraid of suffocation, the fires of the spellblaze or arcane radiation.

Eyalites may be forced to undergo the Onilug transformation as well. It has actually worked out beautifully. Countless half-wit necromancers, too blinded by their own ambition, have willingly come to us, offering their frail Eyalite flesh to undergo the Onilug transformation. Dangle but a drop of power in front of them and they will snap at it like half-starved wolves.

Our onilug researchers continue to elevate the craft of Necromancy to greater heights, designing new undead creatures to unleash in our inevitable invasion of Eyal's surface. It is only a matter of time before their whole world is swept under a tide of the dead.]], [[死靈法術，是曾經在我們的世界上被長期使用的古老藝術。儘管在烏魯洛克的黃金年代裏，人們漸漸廢棄了對死靈法術的使用。但是，隨着夏·圖爾人毀滅了我們的家園，我們重新拾起了我們古老的研究，再次學習使用這一暗黑技藝的方法。

歐尼路格是那些完全將自己獻身給死亡的縞瑪瑙之子。這一轉化的過程恐怖而痛苦，最終，他們成爲了能夠完全適應操縱不死能量的惡魔。他們的肉體變得乾枯憔悴，如同只披着一層皮的骷髏一般。我們向勇於接受這一改造的同胞致敬，是他們的獻身讓我們朝着毀滅埃亞爾的目標更近了一步。

因爲他們已經不再是生者，歐尼路格無需懼怕宇宙的虛空。他們可以在燒焦的大地上游走，不需要呼吸，也不再懼怕魔法大爆炸的火焰和奧術的輻射。

埃亞爾人也可以被迫接受歐尼路格的改造。我們已經產生了不少成功的例子。無數的半吊子死靈法師，被自己的野心矇蔽了雙眼，心甘情願的來到我們面前，獻出自己虛弱的埃亞爾人肉體，接受改造成爲歐尼路格。只要把一點點力量在他們眼前晃動一下，他們就會像餓狼一樣猛撲上來，自尋死路。

我們的歐尼路格研究者，將會繼續把死靈法術的藝術研究到登峯造極，設計出更多更強大的死靈生物，並在我們最終進攻埃亞爾地面的大軍裏釋放出來。只要稍等一點時間，這個世界就會被死者的屍潮席捲。]], "_t")
t("demon statue: wretch titan", "惡魔雕像：腐化泰坦", "_t")
t("The modified children of emerald, known as the Wretchlings, willingly accept their role as the arrows in Urh'Rok's quiver, and most only live to see a couple of engagements before giving their lives in battle.  Once in a great while, though, one will stand toe-to-toe with the enemy and repeatedly come out on top.  These outstanding fighters, chosen by fate and their own talent, are recalled, then put through a series of tests to ensure that their survival was not due to luck alone.  Roughly 70% of these are then assigned to breeding duties, ensuring that the Wretchling bloodline gets ever stronger as it is forged in the fires of combat; the rest, whether due to sterility, consuming too much resources to sustain their brood, or simply insisting on staying in the fights for which they were created, are nurtured to maturity and once again let loose on the battlefield.  If wretchlings are our arrows, wretch titans are our trebuchet boulders, causing a tremendous amount of damage to the enemy line with their incredible strength and the geysers of acid spurting from their flesh.  Although no less aggressive than their younger counterparts, wretch titans generally have a much higher survival rate, due to not only their formidable power and size, but the sheer terror they cause when charging at the enemy - few Eyalites would stand and fight against such a foe, particularly when it means standing in a rapidly-growing pool of acid.", [[綠翡翠的孩子們，酸液樹魔，愉快地接受了作爲烏魯洛克之箭的身份，大部分在戰死前都只能見證幾次戰鬥。但少數情況下，也會有個體在面對面的廝殺中取得持續的勝利。這些卓越的被命運和他們自身天賦選定的近戰專家，將被召回做檢測，以確保並非是全然的幸運令其生存。大約 70%將會投放至生產線，令酸液樹魔的血統更加強壯，更加精於戰鬥。剩下的，不論是因爲無法生育，還是因爲堅持戰鬥本能，將發育成熟而再次出征前線。如果說酸液樹魔是我們的箭矢，那麼腐化泰坦就是我們的投石機，能用無比的力量和猛烈的酸液製造成噸的傷害。他們不比酸液樹魔殺傷力小，同時生存率要高得多——這不僅僅是因爲他們的力量和體積，更是因爲他們面對敵人時製造的恐懼——幾乎無人能站在他們面前肉搏，尤其是在地表上有不斷擴張的強酸池時。
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: dolleg", "惡魔雕像：多雷格", "_t")
t("A walking monument to times of prosperity, the dolleg was once a beast of burden, carrying loads of trade goods through the Sher'Tul portals.  Reliable, friendly, and rather intelligent for a beast, dollegs were often taken in as beloved pets as well - their joyous chirps when seeing their master get home could brighten up anyone's day, and despite their large size they were gentle enough to play with our young.  Their kind temperament and dutiful labor were the pride of our breeding practices, and two-thirds of our population either owned, lived in a home with, or worked with a dolleg.  In the wake of Mal'Rok's destruction, the children of emerald developed an effective process to convert these companions into beasts of war, covered in acidic spines and thick plating, and loyally tearing through our enemies with incredible force.  Unfortunately, their friendly demeanor was lost in order to make them merciless in combat; of all the sacrifices we've had to make for our war, it might be the loss of our gentle companions that troubles us the most.", [[活着的繁榮紀念碑——多雷格曾是負重的野獸，身載貨物經過夏·圖爾傳送門。可信，友善，同時比野獸更有智力，多雷格也一度充當愛寵——當看見主人回家時他們發出的歡鳴能讓人快活一整天，同時，儘管體型龐大，他們動作卻十分溫柔，和孩子們玩耍時也不必擔心。他們溫和的脾性與本分的勞作是我們繁衍中的榮耀，三分之二的人在生活中都有一隻多雷格陪伴，一起工作或者生活。在瑪·洛克毀滅後，綠翡翠的孩子們發明了一種有效的方法將多雷格轉化爲戰爭巨獸，身軀被酸刺與厚甲覆蓋，忠誠驅使他們以巨力猛衝向敵人。不幸的是，他們溫和的舉止在培育其無情戰鬥的能力時喪失殆盡；盡數我們爲戰爭作出的犧牲，失去溫柔夥伴可能是最大、也是最困擾我們的一項。
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: uruivellas", "惡魔雕像：烏爾維拉斯", "_t")
t("The minotaur is one of Eyal's more interesting creatures, and a good example of the devious designs the Sher'Tul had in mind while creating or altering Eyal's races.  Its instincts draw it toward narrow corridors, twisted passages, magical artifacts, and surges of magical energy, resulting in horned beast-men frequently blundering their way into our bases and encampments.  They also seem to soak up empowering magic very readily, and alter their forms accordingly - a typical minotaur is no match for our forces, but occasionally blight will mutate one into an extremely dangerous horror.  Said blighted forms are too unstable for use among our ranks, but with some effort by the children of emerald and ruby, we can give one the gifts of massively increased strength and the ability to unleash waves of flame on our enemies.  While we currently need to keep most of them enthralled to ensure their loyalty, we've recently begun breeding minotaurs on our continent so we can train them from birth to know our cause of righteous revenge - and already some wandering minotaurs accept our cause and our blessings willingly!  It seems the natives of Eyal are no kinder to their own brethren than they are to us.", [[米諾陶是埃亞爾大陸上頗爲神奇的生物，同時也是夏·圖爾人制造或者改變埃亞爾種族的一個絕妙的例子。它的本能吸引它前往狹窄的走廊，扭曲的通道，魔法神器和魔法能量之所在，並相應改變其形態——一隻正常的牛頭人不是我們需要的，不過偶爾枯萎力量能將其變異爲極其危險的恐魔。這些枯萎形態不夠穩定，不能爲我們所用，但經過紅寶石和綠翡翠的孩子們的努力後，我們能將無比的力量與釋放火焰的能力賦予之。我們現在不得不奴役大部分烏爾維拉斯以確保忠誠，同時最近我們也開始在我們的大陸上飼養米諾陶，這樣我們就能從小灌輸我們正義的復仇——已經有部分米諾陶自願接受了我們的理由和祝福！似乎埃亞爾的原住民對其同胞也並不比對我們友善。
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: daelach", "惡魔雕像：達萊奇", "_t")
t("Any one of us who's read up on our history will remember the story of the wicked dust-mages, tormenting us with sentient storms from the safety of their hidden cities.  Although we were tempted at the time to erase all vestiges of their knowledge and culture like they did to us, we knew their magic could come in handy someday, and when their cities lay in ruin, we plundered their libraries for their writings, then dutifully copied down the practical details from these while stripping out the rest.  Once the portals were unleashed on us, the children of ruby (after some controversy) managed to use their old spells to create a new kind of storm, one of swirling flames and coals rather than dust and sand.  Obedient and cheap (if hazardous) to make, these living spells will torment and raze Eyal with their fiery onslaught, like their predecessors once did to Mal'Rok.", "任何讀過我們歷史的人都將銘記塵埃法師的故事，他們躲在隱藏的城市裏，用有感知能力的風暴折磨我們。儘管我們最終抹消了他們所有知識和文化的傳承，正如他們對我們所做的，我們仍清楚地認識到，他們的魔法終有一日會重現。於是，我們在他們城市淪爲廢墟時，奪走了其圖書館內的知識，將有實際價值的內容摘抄下來，其他的統統抹去。當傳送門解開後，紅寶石的孩子們（在矛盾的抉擇後）成功地使用古舊的咒語釋放出全新的風暴——火焰和煤炭代替了塵土和沙子。更加易於製造，這些法術將屠戮生靈，折磨並毀滅埃亞爾大陸，正如它們的前任居民曾經對瑪·洛克做的一樣。", "_t")
t("demon statue: champion of Urh'Rok", "惡魔雕像：烏魯洛克的精英衛兵", "_t")
t("The Divine Tournament of Combat is the most straightforward of our competitions for the spectator, but those competing have a huge variety of possible divisions to enter.  Most are based on the maximum amount of energy consumed by their entrants since (and including) birth; others include those set in an open field for direct combat, or a difficult-to-navigate forest of pillars to properly evaluate those who use hit-and-run tactics or excel at setting up or detecting ambushes.  In the high-energy divisions, those competing are typically not born in the conventional manner, usually being constructs made by a team performing a collaborative effort.  The constructs we now call Champions of Urh'Rok have utterly devastated most of the high-energy open-field divisions, while performing adequately in the less-direct ones, making them a solid fit for production and deployment in the invasion.  Their development team has earned a place of honor for their ingenious methods of creating such incredible strength with a sustainable amount of energy-input, and once mass-production is in order, these gigantic creatures will become the backbone of our military.  Once they arrive on the surface, Eyal will experience a few fleeting moments of terror before their utter annihilation.", [[神聖戰鬥錦標賽是對我們的觀衆來說最爲熟悉的比賽，然而有些人不知道的是，這場錦標賽有非常多的組別。大部分的組別劃分來自於選手從出生開始所消耗的能量，而其他的一些分類方法包括在開放場地的直接戰鬥，亦或是在難以辨認方向的複雜迷宮裏進行，以選拔那些能夠靈活地使用游擊戰術、精巧的發動和判別突襲的選手。在最高能量的組別，那些挑戰者並不是正常出生的天才，而是在各個比賽有關的研究團隊團結合作，精心設計的產物。這些造物現在被我們稱爲烏魯洛克的精英衛兵，他們在高能組的開放場地直接戰鬥領域幾乎所向披靡，在其他複雜的環境下也有相當出色的表現，讓他們可以在未來侵略部隊的組成和部署中發揮極大的作用。製造他們的研究團隊爲他們的偉大創造——通過很少的能量就能創造擁有如此強大力量的造物——獲得了崇高的讚譽。這些巨大的怪物將會成爲我們軍隊的中流砥柱。只要他們組成的軍隊成批到達埃亞爾，那些弱小的生物瞬間就會被他們強大的力量徹底殲滅。
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: forge giant", "惡魔雕像：鍛造巨人", "_t")
t("The power of Urh'Rok cannot be overstated, except by claiming it to be infinite.  Most of his strength and will are occupied at the moment, keeping our shattered home from splintering off into the void; as such, he cannot spend time or effort making equipment for our army.  The children of onyx recognized this, and worked on a way to maximize the amount of benefit they could get from a small portion of his power; Urh'Rok was pleased by their idea, and granted their request in full, giving them a handful of enormous hammers, each one glowing with his magic.  These were then given to modified variants of the Champion of Urh'Rok template, built for raw strength at the expense of speed and energy-efficient creation, and now they work tirelessly, heating raw metal with their magic until it is workable, then pounding it into their shape, automatically imbuing the resulting armor and weaponry with Urh'Rok's blessing.  Thanks to an assortment of detachable heads for these hammers, every single swing produces several pieces of usable equipment.  The constant exposure to the power of Urh'Rok has made these creatures almost absurdly formidable, but as useful as they would be on the front lines, they are even more useful bolstering the rest of our forces with blessed equipment; that said, should our scouting parties encounter a problem that requires drastic and immediate intervention, sending a Forge-Giant down is a reliable emergency option, and would immediately clear up any combat-related difficulties should the situation call for it.", [[要說怎麼形容烏魯洛克大人的強大能力的話，沒有什麼詞語比“無窮無盡”更加合適了。不過不幸的是，由於他大部分的力量和意志都被用於凝聚我們被炸得支離破碎的土地，不讓其飛散到無盡虛空之中；他或許沒有足夠的時間和精力來爲我們的部隊製造裝備。縞瑪瑙之子們意識到了這個問題，找到了一種從父親大人的強大力量中的一小部分最大程度地發揮的方法。烏魯洛克大人認可了他們的提議，製造了一些灌注了他強大魔法力量的巨錘。這些贈禮被帶給一些被改造的烏魯洛克精英衛兵，以犧牲一定行動速度和能量燃率的代價，他們獲得了無與倫比的強大蠻力。他們日夜不停地工作，將金屬的原材料用魔法熔鍊，然後將其導入模具中，自動鍛造成注入了烏魯洛克的祝福的魔鋼武器和護甲。在各種可拆卸的錘頭的幫助下，只要一擊就能瞬間製造出數個裝備零件。長期暴露在烏魯洛克的強大力量下，這些生物擁有可畏的強大力量。然而，與在前線作戰相比，他們更應該留在這裏爲我們的部隊送去支援的裝備。因而，只有在我們的先遣部隊遇到需要立即強大的武力介入的危急時刻，我們纔會向下遣送鍛造巨人，他們強大的力量將會立即掃清戰鬥中所面臨的一切困難。
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: thaurhereg", "惡魔雕像：修爾希瑞格", "_t")
t("Thanks to numerous contacts we have on Eyal's surface, ranging from easily-duped natives to our own scouting teams, we've managed to gain a few captive Eyalites.  These prisoners are useful for a variety of tasks, including manual labor, magical research, stress relief, and developing new methods of torture (those last two often being one in the same).  We try to preserve these temporarily-valuable subjects for as long as we can, but invariably, an experiment goes wrong or someone uses too much force, and the captive ends up mortally wounded.  Rather than let these world-breakers escape their eternal fate by simply dying, we put their bodies and life-essence to use, combining several fallen Eyalites into a creature held together by their collective rage and suffering.  You'd think this would be a bad idea to have walking around our base of operations, but as it turns out, it just takes a few simple enchantments to redirect their vengeful instincts towards their former brethren, making them fearsome and sadistic in combat.  Their rampages against their \"tormentors\" are simply hilarious!", [[源於我們對埃亞爾大陸的多次接觸，從容易受騙的當地傻瓜到我們有組織的探險隊，我們有機會活捉了一些埃亞爾人。這些俘虜能夠用於許多工作，比如苦力、魔法研究、找樂子，以及發明新的酷刑（後兩者通常是同一回事）。我們曾經試圖長期保存這些暫時還是比較珍貴的樣本。不過每一次，只要實驗出了點問題，或者有誰下手的時候稍微沒有掌握好力度，這些樣本就會當場慘死。對於這些破壞世界的邪徒來說，讓他們通過死亡逃離自己永恆折磨的命運實在是太便宜他們了。我們把他們的肢體和生命精華取出，用他們的憤怒和痛苦將幾個埃亞爾人的屍體拼接在一起。你或許覺得讓他們在我們的指揮部附近晃來晃去是個壞主意，不過事實證明，只需要幾個簡單地魔法就可以把他們復仇的強烈衝動轉移到他們曾經的同族身上，讓他們在戰鬥中變得施虐成性、令人望而生畏。看看他們在狂亂中屠殺自己眼中的“敵人”的樣子，還真是讓人忍俊不禁！
]], "_t")
t("demon statue: dúathedlen", "惡魔雕像：多瑟頓", "_t")
t([[#{italic}#This plaque is mostly covered in shifting shadows.  You can only make out a little bit of the text.#{normal}#

#927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#heregs are not the only way we recycle #927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#arness their fear and suspici#927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#outs.  Cautious and yet sadistic, these assassins #927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#markably effective in indirect combat, setting ambus#927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#justice.  Additionally, the shadows they produce #927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#spionage, scouting, and #927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#king them a val#927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST#tion to our intel-gathering camps. Redee#927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST# data they contribute on#927e64#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#LAST# paving the way for our invasion.

#{italic}#As you reach the end, the text goes completely black, and a new message forms.#{normal}#

#{bold}#WE SEE YOU.#{normal}#]], [[#{italic}#上面的文字被浮動的陰影所籠罩，你只能依稀看到模糊的文字碎片#{normal}#

#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～~#LAST#希瑞格並不是我們回收#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～#LAST#卸下他們的恐懼和懷#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～#LAST#。他們已經變得謹慎，然而仍然足夠施虐成性，這些暗夜的殺手#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～~ ～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～#LAST#他們卓越的表現在非直接戰鬥，尤其是發動突#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～#LAST#義。另外，他們製造的黑暗之霧#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～~#LAST#間諜活動，偵察活動，以及#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～~#LAST#給他們一個#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～#LAST#息提供給了我們的情報機構。爲了償#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～~#LAST#他們提供的數據被用#927e64#～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～～~#LAST#爲我們最終的侵略鋪平了道路。

